{"_id":"68a7360a8ec3d8323af115a5","nodeId":"5h7U0spwEUhB-hbjSlaeB","roadmapSlug":"angular","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:50.309Z","description":"# Enforce Trusted Types\n\nIt is recommended that you use Trusted Types as a way to help secure your applications from cross-site scripting attacks. Trusted Types is a web platform feature that can help you prevent cross-site scripting attacks by enforcing safer coding practices. Trusted Types can also help simplify the auditing of application code.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Enforcing Trusted Types","url":"https://angular.dev/best-practices/security#enforcing-trusted-types","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e92"},{"type":"official","title":"W3C - Trusted Types","url":"https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e93"},{"type":"official","title":"Trusted Types API","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Trusted_Types_API","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e94"},{"type":"article","title":"How to use Trusted Types","url":"https://web.dev/articles/trusted-types#how-to-use-trusted-types","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e95"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:01:05.151Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/angular/content/5h7U0spwEUhB-hbjSlaeB.md"}